# pnpm-lock.yaml is machine-generated by pnpm, not hand-authored YAML.
#
# Left to prettier, this file gets rewritten on every commit that touches it:
# pnpm emits single-quoted scalars and no blank lines between importers,
# prettier's YAML printer emits double-quoted scalars with a blank line after
# each key - both valid YAML, same content, so the reformat is pure noise on
# top of whatever dependency actually changed.
#
# It went unnoticed here because every human commit runs pre-commit locally,
# which silently re-normalizes the file to prettier's style before it is ever
# seen. Dependabot commits through GitHub's API and never runs pre-commit, so
# its pull requests showed pnpm's native format against prettier's - a full
# ~1700-line diff for a single dependency version bump, every time.
#
# pnpm, not prettier, owns this file's formatting. `pnpm install` is
# idempotent on it - re-running with no dependency change touches nothing -
# which is the property that actually keeps a lockfile diff reviewable.
pnpm-lock.yaml
